A||N||10||Elenor84||Talk to me about Putting a 305 in with little modifications...||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||06-08-2001||05:36 PM||||Hey guys...tranny is definetly busted...I'm going to replace it with a used one...but...I'm thinking about doing an engine swap at the same time...now I was with my fiero club the other day and I heard that u can drop a 305 in with no modifications to the cradle...just a new heavy duty dog bone and a new fly wheel...is this true?  Do u guys suggest I do this?  Is it as simple as it sounds?  Thx...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||06-08-2001||05:55 PM||||You still have to buy an archie kit.<P>Wish it were that easy. As for a 305. I don't think the weight of the iron head motor warrants the power. You can build up a high HP 305 , but for the money you would be better off to get a 350. Most 305's you will find (perhaps all?) have between 130 and 150hp.. Not the greatest but not too shabby<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||06-08-2001||05:56 PM||||Alright...thank you very much...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fyerstarter||06-08-2001||11:13 PM||||Um when compared to the stock V6 which has between 130-150 hp and weighs a helluva lot less and fits right in whats the point?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||06-09-2001||03:35 AM||||Yeah, 305 and 350 swaps are the same.  They're both Small Block Chevy's.  No real advantage to the 305, unless it's real cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||06-09-2001||11:38 AM||||I have yet to see a 305 respond well to improvements,very doggy motor.<BR>Maybe think about a pushrod 3.4,or a TDC if you're into wiring things,and making your own exhaust.They're pretty much the true bolt-ins.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Elenor84||06-09-2001||11:59 PM||||Are u saying I can put a 3.4 litre in with no expensive kit?  The sit rap is that I need a new tranny...but I'm thinking of throwing a new engine in as well...now...I can either just get an engine tranny combo with 127,000 kilometers...(2.5 litre)(4speed)...exact same...or I can get a tranny and then put a better engine in...but I don't want to spend more then about 800 bucks...tranny being around 100 I only have 700 left for engine...any idea's?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||voyagerspe||06-10-2001||12:17 AM||||im planning on putting a 305 TPI motor in my 88 formula fiero.  its an 86 motor out of a transam 190 hp 265 lb torque(at the rear wheels in a gm f-body).  I originally bought the motor for the TPI setup and was planning to use it on a 350 but this 305 is just a super smooth running engine. with minimal mods ill have this engine in the 250 to 270 hp range.  <BR>my point is you can get much more than 150 hp <BR>out of a 305.  Also in a F-body the milage is in the low 20's in a fiero mileage and HP should be much higher.<BR>I realize that "cubes are king" and if you want power go with the biggest engine you can shoehorn into that engine compartment.  But I had to come to the defence of the 305.  <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||06-10-2001||01:08 AM||||I had a 86 Trans Am with the L69 305 and would love to have a similar motor in a Fiero. Yes a 350 would be great, but I wouldn't disrespect a 305.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT-maniac||06-10-2001||04:35 PM||||Well I think the only way your going to get a new motor put in for 800 bucks is if you replace it with another 4 banger. A used 2.8 was around $ 500 here in Alberta when I phoned around for one a couple of months ago and nobody had one then. They wanted 6 - 700 for a 3.4. By the time you get the motor and the new clutch you might as well put in you're looking at around $ 650.00. So you'd only have a little left to buy all the parts that get broken or lost during the switch, and only if you did it yourself. Plus if you go for a non stock motor you'll have all the extra cost of adapting everything to work. It can be done of course but it won't be cheap. I've got a dead 2.8 block you could have if you want to rebuild one.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Butter||06-11-2001||11:09 AM||||Yes, a v8 kit is required to insert a 305 into a Fiero.  305 was the last v8 I had in my Fiero.  For the folks who think a 305 ain't got no pep, well you folks ain't holdin' your mouth right when you put it together.  ||||reg||7
